# Lock-cleanup and git-lock debris (item diagnostic, 2026-10-14, run 194).
# Confirmed directly in the Cowork sandbox: unlink() on this FUSE-mounted
# working copy returns EPERM even on a file this session just created itself,
# while rename() and truncate() both succeed. That is a real, reproducible
# property of this mount, not a one-off or a Windows-side artefact. Every
# earlier run's "clear a stale lock by renaming/overwriting it" workaround was
# therefore correct, but each rename or probe file it left behind (to
# characterise the bug afresh) became a new piece of untracked debris,
# because nothing told git to stop caring about that shape of filename.
# These patterns are root-anchored (leading /) so they cannot catch a
# similarly-named file deliberately placed inside tools/, modules/ etc.
/.agent-lock.*
/.AGENT_LOG_*.md
/.tmp_log_combined.md
/AGENT_LOG.md.restored
/AGENT_LOG.md.testprobe
/.new_entry_*.md
/.new-entry-*.md
/.new-log-entry.md.done
/.scratch_entry.md
/.scratch_qsummary.txt
/.scratch-probe-test.tmp
/.scratch_audit/
/.git-junk-quarantine/
/.git-lock-debris-quarantine/
/.git-lock-debris-quarantine-local-only/
/.probe*
/._probe*
/.canary-test*
/.delete-test*
/.delete-canary*
/.lock-test*
/.lock_test*
/.rm-test*
/.runtest-*
/.unlink*
/.write-test*
/.zzz-test*
/.zzz_test*
/test_overwrite_probe*
/testfile*
/testwrite*
/testperm*
/testnew*
/newtestfile.txt
/scratch_a.txt
/b_test_dst.txt
/zz_test_delete.txt
/zzz_test_add_check.txt
/_delete_test_123.txt
/CLAUDE.md.probe
/.commit-test-probe.txt*
/.git-test-add-probe-*
/C:/
*.cleared-*
*.released-*
*.aside-*
*.movedaside-*
*.recovered-*
*.REMOVED-*
*.moved-ok
*.stale-*
*.used-*
/._tmp_entry_*.md
/.test-probe-*
/test_write.tmp

# Same AGENT_LOG-repair debris as above but without the leading dot, found by
# check-postcodes.js on the 2026-10-19 quality-pass re-run (run 308): both
# files carry fabricated placeholder postcodes (ZZ11 1ZZ, L9 8CD) from a
# prior run's log-concatenation attempt, not real content.
/AGENT_LOG_NEW_267.md
/AGENT_LOG_combined_scratch.md

# The ".__" double-underscore prefix is the dominant shape of debris this
# EPERM-on-unlink bug (Q134) has produced since run214: probe files, cleared
# locks, scratch log entries, diagnostic markers. Two of them
# (.__combined_run214.md, .__pending_entry_for_log.md) carry the same
# fabricated placeholder postcodes as AGENT_LOG_combined_scratch.md above and
# have been failing check-postcodes.js on every quality pass since at least
# run283 (2026-11-08 04:42 UTC) purely because nothing told git, or the
# checker's gitignore-driven debris filter, to stop caring about this shape
# of filename - the same gap the rest of this file already closed for every
# other debris shape. Root-anchored so it cannot catch a deliberately placed
# file of this name inside tools/, modules/ etc. Added on the 2026-11-08
# 07:43 UTC quality pass (run286) specifically to retire this one recurring
# false failure; 38 pre-existing untracked ".__*" files in the repo root
# were never trackable in the first place (EPERM blocks `git rm` too) so this
# only stops git and the checkers minding them, it does not remove them.
/.__*
